# Privacy Policy — Bhagavad Gita

_Last updated: 2026-07-08_

Bhagavad Gita ("the app", package `com.coretility.bhagavadgita`) is designed to be private by
default. This policy explains what the app does and does not do with your information.

## Data we collect
**No personal data.** We do not collect your name, email, contacts, location, or any content you
create (notes, collections, reading history).

**Anonymous usage analytics.** When enabled (Settings → Privacy → "Share anonymous usage data",
on by default), the app sends anonymous, aggregated interaction events to Google Firebase
Analytics — e.g. that a verse was viewed (chapter/verse number), commentary was expanded, audio was
played, or a search returned N results.

Never sent: your notes, the text you type into search, which verses you liked/saved, your reading
history, or any identifier that names you. Search is logged only as a length and a result count.

You can turn analytics off at any time in Settings → Privacy. Analytics are processed by Google as
our processor (see the Google Privacy Policy and Firebase privacy documentation). No advertising
identifiers are used.

## Data stored on your device
All of your activity — reading progress, likes, saved verses, collections, personal notes, reading
streaks, and settings — is stored **only on your device** using local storage (an on-device
database and preferences). This information never leaves your device and is not sent to us or any
third party.

If you uninstall the app, this locally stored data is removed by the operating system.

## Network access
The app is fully functional offline — the entire scripture ships inside it. There is no account and
no advertising. Besides the optional analytics described above, network access happens only when you
explicitly act (sharing a verse to an app you choose, opening an external link, or rating the app).

## Notifications
If you enable the optional daily "Verse of the Day" reminder, the notification is scheduled locally
on your device. No notification data is sent to any server.

## Content & attribution
Scripture text is derived from the open-source `gita/gita` dataset, released into the public domain
under The Unlicense. Translations and commentaries are displayed with author attribution.

## Children's privacy
The app is suitable for all ages and does not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, including
children.

